ate in presidential politics, with a partisan lean of about six points toward the GOP and no Democratic win at the top of the ticket in decades. With the incumbent president term-limited, both parties face an open field, and no candidate-specific polling, fundraising figures, or expert ratings are yet available for this race.\n\nRecent coverage has framed Alaska as a potential future swing state, pointing to Democratic competitiveness in down-ballot races and a broader midterm surge. That narrative suggests the state may be more competitive than its baseline lean, but it has not yet been tested in a presidential context. The forecast therefore starts from the state's fundamental Republican edge, with wide uncertainty reflecting the absence of polls and ratings.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2436, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3013, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2918, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.3121, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2994, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.311, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2901, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2902, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2863, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2839, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.2961, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.2887, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.3221, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.316, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.3428, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.2873, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.3381, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.2828, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.2931, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.3125, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.2841, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-1